        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Orpington\n- Organizations: House of Commons of the UK Parliament, Conservative Party\n- People: Jo Johnson, Boris Johnson\n- Roles: Member of Parliament, Minister for Universities and Science\n- Events: 1945 creation of the constituency, 2015 general election\n\nFacts:\n- Orpington is a UK Parliament constituency that was created in 1945.\n- Jo Johnson was born on 23 December 1971.\n- Jo Johnson is a British politician in the Conservative Party.\n- Orpington has been represented in the House of Commons of the UK Parliament by Jo Johnson since 2010.\n- Jo Johnson is the brother of Boris Johnson.\n- Following the May 2015 general election, Jo Johnson became Minister for Universities and Science.",
